.TH SDL_GPUPrimitiveType 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GPUPrimitiveType \- Specifies the primitive topology of a graphics pipeline.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_GPUPrimitiveType
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_GPU_PRIMITIVETYPE_TRIANGLELIST,  /**< A series of separate triangles. */
.BI "    SDL_GPU_PRIMITIVETYPE_TRIANGLESTRIP, /**< A series of connected triangles. */
.BI "    SDL_GPU_PRIMITIVETYPE_LINELIST,      /**< A series of separate lines. */
.BI "    SDL_GPU_PRIMITIVETYPE_LINESTRIP,     /**< A series of connected lines. */
.BI "    SDL_GPU_PRIMITIVETYPE_POINTLIST      /**< A series of separate points. */
.BI "} SDL_GPUPrimitiveType;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If you are using POINTLIST you must include a point size output in the vertex shader\[char46]
.PP

\(bu For HLSL compiling to SPIRV you must decorate a float output with [[vk::builtin(\(dqPointSize\(dq)]]\[char46]
.PP
\(bu For GLSL you must set the gl_PointSize builtin\[char46]
.PP
\(bu For MSL you must include a float output with the [[point_size]] decorator\[char46]
.PP
Note that sized point topology is totally unsupported on D3D12\[char46] Any size other than 1 will be ignored\[char46] In general, you should avoid using point topology for both compatibility and performance reasons\[char46] You WILL regret using it\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateGPUGraphicsPipeline (3)
